From 9d619aeac9eb569431d01580b00d6d0a159f7a1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:54:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: rename baseline packs to mcchanges and add Bedrock
 Edition mcchanges jars

Rename the baseline pack feature to mcchanges: the options are now
mcchanges_path, mcchanges_version and skip_language_keys_identical_to_mcchanges,
and the version index of a jar with many versions is mcchanges.json.

Rewrite build_mcchanges_jar.py so that one command downloads, packs and
verifies the jar. It supports Java Edition (Mojang releases and asset index)
and Bedrock Edition (Mojang/bedrock-samples releases), and --update appends
new versions with the same result as a full rebuild. Each version is compared
with the version before it.

Support ZIP64 archives in the ZIP reader, so a jar with more than 65535
entries can be read. Update the documentation.
